From 239bea020909fba0a45e66d8cec7233d727b595e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 02:06:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rd: Vulkan setting, resolution held to the device, SMAA in
 the dark, look up, FOV in degrees, wetter wet look

- Settings > Display > Graphics API (keys.ini graphics_api = auto | vulkan | dx12): PS2_GPU_BACKEND=vulkan-first / dx12-first,
  the other API when the first cannot start; auto picks Vulkan first above 4x
- the inner resolution held to what the device binds of one buffer (Direct3D 12: 128 MB, 4x); 5x and up failed every bind group
- SMAA's edge test on a square-root brightness curve (dark pictures had almost no edges past the threshold)
- PS2_PRESENT_DUMP=<vblank>,<file.ppm>: the picture as the window gets it, with SMAA's edges and weights
- host call 203 (PS2_CAMERA_FRAME, Raw Danger's own by default): the camera's step run by the host, the view tilted up past the ground
- field of view in degrees across (keys.ini field_of_view = ps2 | N deg; old per cent values converted), more steps, the degree sign
- the wet look stronger (it runs after the colour filter since 0047)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
